{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"After escalation, an unavailable implementer can cause the run to repeat work on an exhausted model instead of stopping when the pinned chain is used up."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An environment-blocked verification retry can repeat the same model and stop without trying the available alternative."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The warning attributes the repeated verifier to the implementer even when the excluded model was the previous verifier."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A pinned decision chain discards a usable last-resort answer and unnecessarily requires human intervention."},{"id":"C3b","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The warning attributes a finder-vendor match to the implementer, misleading the operator about the overridden preference."},{"id":"C6b","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The completed-review message can claim no other vendor was available even when pinned routing selected among available alternatives."}]}